CORE symex-driven-lazy-loading-expected-failure
Test
-cp target/classes --function Test.check --full-slice
^\[java::Test\.check:\(I\)V\.assertion\.1\] line 3 .*: FAILURE$
^\[java::Test\.check:\(I\)V\.assertion\.2\] line 5 .*: SUCCESS$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
A failing Java assertion ends the path with ASSUME false. The full slicer must
keep it, else the second assertion becomes reachable with x == 7.
